    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:46.876Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Claim\n\nAttributable skill execution does not require new agent capabilities. It requires three conventions:\n\n1. Skills declare the document models they operate on and the actions they may emit\n2. The agent runtime dispatches skill outputs as actions, not raw text or unstructured tool calls\n3. Artifacts are document-model documents (schema + operation log)\n\n## Cost vs payoff\n\nModest discipline at the skill/runtime boundary; structural payoff for evaluation (process auditing), safety (attribution), and knowledge claims (falsifiability via \"how was this made?\").",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-16T20:32:46.876Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:46.876Z"
    }
  },
